   "text": {
    "L1": "A shadow forms when an object blocks light. It is the dark area where the light cannot reach.",
    "L2": "Here is a common idea: a shadow is longest at noon. That is not true.",
    "L3": "In the morning, the Sun is low in the east, so a shadow is long and points west.",
    "L4": "Around noon, the Sun is high. The shadow is shortest then.",
    "L5": "In the evening, the Sun is low in the west, so the shadow gets long again and points east.",
    "L6": "The Sun only seems to move across the sky because the Earth is spinning. Never look straight at the Sun.",
    "L7": "Now tap the time when the shadow mark is closest to the stick."
   },
